- Always research & plan before coding: search docs, digest hierarchy, base on ground truth
- PLAN course of action after gathering reference info
- Code style: super dry, lean, modular, pythonic, pydantic, NetworkX for in-memory graph
- Lint with Ruff after changes: `ruff check <file_path>` — only changed files
- Always run tests after changes: `python -m pytest kg_engine/tests/ -v`
- Never break existing code; avoid unnecessary try-catches and hardcoded fallbacks

## Domain: Materials Knowledge Graph

Architecture: hybrid graph + vector search (NetworkX in-memory + embeddings for semantic retrieval)
Answer queries like: "что уже делали по сплавам X при режиме Y и какой был эффект на свойство Z"

### 8 Entity Types
MATERIAL, PROPERTY, EXPERIMENT, MODE, EQUIPMENT, TEAM, ARTICLE, CONCLUSION

### 12 Relation Types
HAS_PROPERTY, USED_IN, MEASURES, USES_EQUIPMENT, HAS_MODE, CONDUCTED_BY,
DESCRIBED_IN, HAS_CONCLUSION, DEPENDS_ON, COMPOSED_OF, COMPARED_TO, OPTIMIZED_FOR

### Key Patterns
- Extraction: regex first, LLM fallback for complex relations
- Storage: NetworkX Graph, Pydantic schemas, JSON serialization
- Query: read-only query interface, hybrid search (vector + graph traversal)
- Pipeline: index → ask → find_gaps → save/load
- Tools: LangChain @tool decorated with Pydantic args_schema
- Gap analysis: find missing relations, unconnected entities, sparse subgraphs

